"tourism_types": ["Медико-оздоровчий туризм", "Розважальний туризм", "Спортивний туризм", "Сільський та зелений туризм"], "description_en": "<p>The Tyligul estuary is one of the most impressive natural pearls of the south of Ukraine, where endless steppes meet the clear waters of the estuary, and unique landscapes create a true paradise for lovers of nature, active recreation and gastronomic discoveries.</p>", "detailed_info_en": "<p>The regional landscape park \\"Tiligulskyi\\" covers one of the most valuable nature conservation areas of the country, which stretches between Odesa and Mykolaiv regions. This is a place where nature has been preserved almost in its original form, and every season opens up new colors and impressions.</p><p>Tiligul estuary, almost 60 kilometers long, is one of the cleanest estuaries in Ukraine. Its picturesque shores, steppe slopes, sandy spits and quiet bays form a unique natural landscape that cannot be confused with any other part of the country. It is here that you can see a harmonious combination of marine, steppe and wetland ecosystems that create a special world of wildlife.</p><p>The park is a real paradise for birdwatchers. Every year, thousands of migratory birds choose the Tyligul estuary as a place of rest and nesting. Herons, waders, waders, quacks and dozens of other species turn the territory into one of the most interesting ornithological locations of Ukraine.</p><p>In the spring, the steppes around the estuary are covered with a carpet of rare flowers, among which you can see saffron, hollyhock, snowdrops, and honeysuckle. Many representatives of the local flora are listed in the Red Book of Ukraine, which emphasizes the exceptional conservation value of the territory.</p><p>Tyligul Park offers many opportunities for recreation and travel. Ecological routes, photo tours, wildlife watching, fishing, coastal walks and natural attractions allow you to discover this region from different angles. Uncrowded beaches and wide n