and technology of winemaking: from ancient underground storages up to 9 meters deep to the modern \\"House of Sparkling Wines\\". Visitors can see the full cycle of production — from grape harvesting to bottling, walk through the territory with art objects, visit the Labyrinth Museum and the Fountain of Dionysus, as well as immerse themselves in the atmosphere of a multimedia show about the history of Swiss immigrants. A special highlight of \\"Shabo\\" is professional tastings of premium wines and cognacs in the crystal hall accompanied by a sommelier, as well as the opportunity to see the unique autochthonous grape variety Telti-Kuruk - a true symbol of the region's wine heritage. It is a place where gastronomy, aesthetics and emotions combine to create a profound tourist experience. \\"Shabo\\" is ideal for walking through vineyards, photo tourism, educational tours and wine tastings. The best time to visit is during the autumn harvest or the green summer season, when the vineyards look particularly spectacular. This is not just a tourist attraction, but a real world of wine that should be experienced in person.</p>"}	\N	2026-06-08 11:47:18.122946+00
