но поєднується з живою духовною традицією.</p>", "tourism_types": ["Релігійний туризм"], "description_en": "<p>The Church of the Assumption of the Blessed Virgin Mary in Tatarbunary is a spiritual and historical landmark of southern Bessarabia. Built in 1877 on the site of the first wooden church, the church has been a center of faith, spirituality and cultural heritage of the community for more than a century.</p>", "hero_font_size": null, "reel_image_url": null, "detailed_info_en": "<p>The majestic building in the shape of a cross attracts attention with its blue walls and golden domes, which have become a recognizable architectural decoration of the city. Of special value is the belfry with six bells, among which a bell weighing about 720 kilograms, donated to the church in the 19th century, has been preserved. The Church of the Assumption is one of the few churches in Bessarabia, which continued to function even in the Soviet period, without ceasing services. For many years, a school and a shelter for the needy functioned at the temple, which emphasizes its important role in the life of the local community. Today, the church remains an active spiritual center of Tatarbunar, attracting pilgrims, tourists and anyone interested in the history, architecture and cultural heritage of Odesa. This is a place where centuries-old history is harmoniously combined with a living spiritual tradition.</p>"}	\N	2026-06-11 13:46:49.862931+00
