seum of History and Local Lore is a place where more than two thousand years of the history of the Danube region come to life in real artifacts, documents and human stories. Housed in an ancient building of the 19th century, the museum opens to visitors the fascinating world of one of the oldest cities of Ukraine — Kilia, which for centuries was an important trade and cultural center on the Danube.</p>", "hero_font_size": null, "reel_image_url": null, "detailed_info_en": "<p>During the tour, guests can take a real journey through time: from ancient settlements and the Byzantine era to Cossack times, Russian-Turkish wars and events of the 20th century. The expositions tell about the peoples, cultures and states that left their mark on this land, forming the unique multicultural face of the Ukrainian Danube region. The special atmosphere of the museum is created by the historical building of the former merchant estate, where each hall preserves the spirit of the past. Here you can see old household items, archival documents, photographs and materials that reveal little-known pages of the history of the region and the life of its inhabitants. A visit to the Kili Historical and Local History Museum will be a great addition to your trip to the Danube. This is an opportunity not only to get acquainted with the history of one of the most interesting regions of Odesa, but also to feel the true character of Kilia - a city where different cultures, traditions and eras meet.</p>"}	\N	2026-06-15 08:25:20.177307+00
